      "final_text": "## Setup\n\nExponent in binary: **8432 = 8192 + 128 + 64 + 32 + 16 = 2\u00b9\u00b3 + 2\u2077 + 2\u2076 + 2\u2075 + 2\u2074**\n\nSo I need the repeated squares 7^(2^k) mod 5557 for k = 0\u202613, then multiply the five marked ones.\n\n## Squaring chain (mod 5557)\n\n| k | 7^(2^k) mod 5557 | computation |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 7 | \u2014 |\n| 1 | 49 | 7\u00b2 = 49 |\n| 2 | 2401 | 49\u00b2 = 2401 |\n| 3 | 2192 | 2401\u00b2 = 5,764,801 = 1037\u00b75557 + 2192 |\n| 4 \u2605 | 3616 | 2192\u00b2 = 4,804,864 = 864\u00b75557 + 3616 |\n| 5 \u2605 | 5392 | 3616\u00b2 = 13,075,456 = 2352\u00b75557 + 5392 |\n| 6 \u2605 | 4997 | 5392\u00b2 \u2261 (\u2212165)\u00b2 = 27,225 = 4\u00b75557 + 4997 |\n| 7 \u2605 | 2408 | 4997\u00b2 \u2261 (\u2212560)\u00b2 = 313,600 = 56\u00b75557 + 2408 |\n| 8 | 2513 | 2408\u00b2 = 5,798,464 = 1043\u00b75557 + 2513 |\n| 9 | 2417 | 2513\u00b2 = 6,315,169 = 1136\u00b75557 + 2417 |\n| 10 | 1482 | 2417\u00b2 = 5,841,889 = 1051\u00b75557 + 1482 |\n| 11 | 1309 | 1482\u00b2 = 2,196,324 = 395\u00b75557 + 1309 |\n| 12 | 1925 | 1309\u00b2 = 1,713,481 = 308\u00b75557 + 1925 |\n| 13 \u2605 | 4663 | 1925\u00b2 = 3,705,625 = 666\u00b75557 + 4663 |\n\n\u2605 = bit set in 8432.\n\n## Combining the marked terms\n\n- 3616 \u00b7 5392 = 19,497,472 = 3508\u00b75557 + **3516**\n- 3516 \u00b7 4997 = 17,569,452 = 3161\u00b75557 + **3775**\n- 3775 \u00b7 2408 = 9,090,200 = 1635\u00b75557 + **4505**\n- 4505 \u00b7 4663 = 21,006,815 = 3780\u00b75557 + **1355**\n\n(5557 is prime, so as a cross-check the exponent reduces to 8432 mod 5556 = 2876; the same chain on 2876 = 2048+512+256+32+16+8+4 gives the identical result.)\n\n**1355**"
